## Does Your Pedicure Have to Match Your Fall Manicure?

No. Your pedicure color does not need to match your manicure this fall, and most nail pros will tell you the "matchy" rule is outdated. What matters more is whether the two tones feel coordinated, not identical, since a burgundy mani with a chocolate brown pedi reads just as put together as an exact match.

Toes and fingers live different lives. Fingers get seen constantly, in every gesture and handshake, so a lot of women play it safer there. Toes spend most of the season tucked inside socks and boots, which frees them up to be the bolder half of the pairing. If your fingers are in a soft taupe for the office, your toes can hold a moody forest green with zero conflict. The two don't need to be twins. They need to share a season.

Where the "must match" instinct still holds some water: formal events. A wedding, a big dinner, anything with open-toe heels and full visibility calls for tones that clearly belong to the same family, even if they're not the exact same bottle. For everyday fall life, though, this is one rule you're free to break. If you want a companion guide for the finger side of this equation, our <a href="/blog/fall/fall-nail-colors">fall nail colors</a> roundup breaks down the manicure shades built for the same season.

