## Unexpected Greens for a Modern Fall Pedicure

Olive and forest green have quietly become two of the most requested <strong>fall pedicure colors</strong> among people who already own every brown and red in their collection and want something new that still fits the season.

Olive works because it borrows from the same earthy palette as the rest of fall, just from a different color family entirely. It pairs with rust, camel, and cream in a way that feels considered rather than random. Forest green goes darker and moodier, closer in weight to the deep reds and berries already on this list, which makes it an easy swap for anyone who's tired of merlot but not ready to leave the "moody" category behind.

Both shades photograph particularly well against tan or olive skin, where the green's cooler undertone creates a flattering contrast rather than clashing. On paler skin, a slightly warmer, more olive-leaning green tends to work better than a true cool forest shade. Either way, this is the pick for someone who wants to look like they thought about it, without picking anything predictable.

