## Metallics and Shimmer for Toes This Season

Antique gold, not bright gold. That distinction is the whole story with this <strong>fall pedicure colors</strong> category this year. A softer, more vintage-inspired metallic reads as refined in a way a loud, high-shine gold never quite manages.

Bronze shimmer follows the same logic, adding warmth and dimension without tipping into costume-jewelry territory. On toes, metallics work best as either a full statement pedicure or a subtle accent, a single toe in shimmer against a matte neutral on the rest. Gunmetal, a darker, more industrial cousin of silver, gives the same effect with a moodier finish for anyone who wants shine without brightness.

Metallic polish behaves differently from cream or matte formulas. It shows brush strokes more visibly, so thin, even coats matter here more than almost anywhere else on this list. A gel base helps the shimmer particles sit flat and even, which is worth the extra step if a full metallic pedicure is the goal rather than an accent nail.

